From 00e2dd0605fd2d05448346fe3183a6c1cae968aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:12:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] megatron: failure forensics, HBM spill check and NCCL
 warm-up

Three opt-in helpers for the Megatron worker, all off unless their
environment variables are set:
- failure_forensics: per-rank phase tracking and a dump (stacks, CUDA
  memory, optional memory history) when train or get_logprobs raises
  (NRL_FORENSICS_DIR, NRL_MEM_HISTORY, NRL_MEM_SAMPLE_S).
- hbm_spill: checks whether CPU-offloaded optimizer state landed in GPU
  HBM on GH200 and can bind it to CPU memory (NRL_HBM_SPILL_CHECK,
  NRL_HBM_BIND_CPU).
- nccl_warmup: builds the NCCL communicators right after setup, so a
  slow first collective does not hit the first training step
  (NRL_NCCL_WARMUP).
---
